From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cros-disks: mounts belong to the NickelOS session's user

A NickelOS local account's session runs Chrome and the user's apps as the
account's Linux user (uid 5000-5999), but cros-disks made every mount for
the user owned by chronos: removable media (FAT, exFAT, NTFS, ISO/UDF,
HFS+), archives, FuseBox (the Files app) and SFTP mounts. The user could
read a USB stick but not write to it.

When a session starts, cros-disks now asks session_manager for the
session's account and, for a local account (<name>@nickel.localhost),
makes mounts owned by that Linux user; group chronos-access is unchanged.
cros-disks' D-Bus policy lets it make that one call.
Any other session, and the time without one, keeps chronos. The
removable-media mounters are rebuilt when the owner changes.

---
diff -ruN a/cros-disks/archive_mounter.cc b/cros-disks/archive_mounter.cc
--- a/cros-disks/archive_mounter.cc
+++ b/cros-disks/archive_mounter.cc
